1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,650
This is the Sungu Duri.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,920
People also call it
the pufferfish thorn,

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,650
because we live by the coast,
by the beach.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,420
Calling it pufferfish thorn is fine too.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,250
But outsiders, tourists, they say

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:19,250
this is a durian, a durian basket.
That's what they say.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,850
But in my community,
long ago, in the old days,

8
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,550
things that had been blessed
were placed inside it.

9
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,950
Because it has these thorns,

10
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:37,300
evil things outside
will not disturb what is inside,

11
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,800
Before this, sungu duri did not have thorns

12
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,520
It had no thorn like these,
it was just plain.

13
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,800
Because there were thorn
on other products,

14
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:50,200
for example the ones my late mother made,

15
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:55,020
so that evil ones would not disturb them,
she said.

16
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:58,670
So this Sungu Duri, I learned it
before it had thorn,

17
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:00,800
and I made the thorn like this.

18
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:04,970
It is related to mengkuang.
Among the many kinds of mengkuang,

19
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:08,600
only selected mengkuang is used
to make this Sungu Duri.

20
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:13,770
The technique is called anyaman gila
(the "crazy weave").

21
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:17,870
At the very beginning,
before it becomes a Sungu Duri,

22
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:22,950
we use the anyaman (weaving) gila technique.

23
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,500
For example, the middle here
is also anyaman gila.

24
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,500
We continue with Jawi Anyaman (weaving).

25
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:32,020
And the shape, these thorns,
I have upgraded them.

26
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,050
In truth the Sungu Duri
could have been lost to time.

27
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:39,850
Now I have upgraded it
so that it becomes a present-day ornament.

28
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,550
The sungu was a container for keeping things
in the old days.

29
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,070
Today it is more of
a home decoration, a souvenir,

30
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:52,550
and become tourist product.

31
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:55,850
The hardest part is shaping the spines.

32
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:01,750
If the pulling is not even
and not strong enough,

33
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,550
the thorn will tilt,

34
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,450
and the whole sungu becomes unbalanced.

35
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,350
This is the Sungu Duri,

36
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,350
the cultural identity and heritage
of the Mah Meri.

